      "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe gfx1151 image lacks the AMD SMI Python package. Diffusion platform detection therefore falls back to CPU even when PyTorch sees the HIP device.\n\nThis change restores automatic ROCm detection and enables the AITER configuration validated with FLUX.3.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Install the ROCm-bundled package from /opt/rocm/share/amd_smi and verify import amdsmi during the build.\n- Change the image default to ENV SGLANG_USE_AITER=1.\n- Update the LLM Triton example to explicitly set SGLANG_USE_AITER=0 alongside --attention-backend triton.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nValidation used Radeon 8060S Graphics, gfx1151, with PyTorch 2.9.1 and ROCm 7.2.4.\n\nThe built image selects ROCm without a platform override. A controlled check that blocks the amdsmi import reproduces the CPU fallback.\n\nThe FLUX.3 smoke used these settings:\n\n| Setting | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Model | black-forest-labs/flux-3-image-klein |\n| Attention backend | aiter |\n| Resolution | 1024×1024 |\n| Inference steps | 16 |\n| Concurrency | 1 |\n| Warmup requests | 1 |\n| Measured requests | 5 |\n\nAll six images decoded successfully. Logs record the AITER BF16 varlen attention kernel build and import.\n\nThe full inference smoke used `-e SGLANG_USE_AITER=1`. A separate image derived from the tested build with only the ENV change confirms that AITER is enabled without a runtime override.\n\nCI and model accuracy evaluation were not run.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nThe measurements exclude the warmup request.\n\nRun on\n```python\npython3 -m sglang.multimodal_gen.benchmarks.bench_serving \\\n  --port 30000 \\\n  --task text-to-image \\\n  --dataset vbench \\\n  --width 1024 --height 1024 \\\n  --num-inference-steps 16 \\\n  --warmup-requests 1 \\\n  --warmup-inference-steps 16 \\\n  --num-prompts 5 \\\n  --max-concurrency 1 \\\n  --output-file /tmp/flux3_amdsmi_fix_bench.json\n\n```\n| Metric | Result |\n|---|---:|\n| Completed requests | 5 |\n| Failed requests | 0 |\n| Mean client latency | 82.25 s |\n| Median client latency | 32.25 s |\n| Peak GPU memory | 21,064 MB |\n\nThe first measured request was slow, which raised the mean latency. No matched SDPA comparison was run, so these smoke results do not establish a speedup.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> `SGLANG_USE_AITER=1` changes the default for the entire image. Validation covers FLUX.3 only. The LLM Triton example explicitly sets `SGLANG_USE_AITER=0`. Wan 2.2 enablement with AITER on gfx1151 will be tested and measured separately in a follow-up.\n\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [ ] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #41868413486](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41868413486)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41868412986](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41868412986)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
